1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,080
A Harbor board member asks Morgan what the preparation agent actually did for the proposed session.

2
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:08,720
Morgan could hand over the entire trace.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,820
That would reveal source notes and internal deliberation the board member did not request.

4
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:16,600
Morgan could write a polished story from memory.

5
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:18,160
That would be hard to check.

6
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:27,300
We need a smaller packet: enough to show the boundary, the work, the hold, and the human decision, without dragging every underlying record into the room.

7
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:35,960
Chapter Twenty-One's Scoped Proof Loop has six fields: audience, scope, window, exclusions, export, and ledger.

8
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:42,240
For the Harbor board reader, scope is one session-option paper case across one course planning window.

9
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:52,400
Include the permitted job, evidence-status summary, handoff result, the staffing hold, Morgan's paper disposition, and the still-unapproved print request.

10
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:59,120
Exclude raw source text, prompts, private reasoning, unrelated people, and any actual records.

11
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:01,900
The packet records what is known and what is withheld.

12
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:05,900
It does not certify agent quality or imply a session happened.

13
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:15,880
The workbook calls for capability boundaries, scoped trace references, approval decisions, cost authority summary, export metadata, and reviewer notes.

14
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:20,040
Use course references and a course timestamp label, not a real log.

15
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:23,500
Morgan reviews the proposed proof packet before any sharing.

16
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,620
If a field cannot be safely summarized, mark it withheld with a reason.

17
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:31,540
Redaction is a decision, not a blur laid over a screenshot.

18
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:35,960
Here, the export is only a classroom outline; nothing is sent.

19
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:42,740
The same team then hears an idea: a tiny phone tool that helps volunteer coordinators compare workshop options.

20
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:45,960
The temptation is to build it because it fits the Harbor story.

21
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:56,840
Chapter Twenty-Two asks for a Foundry Test first: demand, monetization, builder fit, build velocity, differentiation, release readiness, and approval gates.

22
00:01:57,420 --> 00:02:00,140
The workbook proposes a weighted score out of one hundred.

23
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,020
A score is useful only when each field has attributable evidence.

24
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:08,640
Our class has no real market research, payer interview, or release review.

25
00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:10,660
Those fields stay unscored.

26
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:14,060
A number without evidence would turn an idea into false proof.

27
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:21,040
Write the smallest safe next test: Morgan could ask for permission to research public demand and clarify who would pay.

28
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:25,000
Even that is a proposed plan, not a provider call or outreach.

29
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:32,760
No repository, tester invite, user data collection, price, store listing, or public claim follows from this lesson.

30
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:37,460
A phone can display the packet and a hold status, but it cannot waive the gate.

31
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:40,820
The valuable outcome may be a decision to shelve the idea.

32
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:43,440
That saves time a rushed build would consume.

33
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:44,280
Pause.

34
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:48,120
What would you leave out of the board packet even if it helped tell a better story?

35
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:52,240
Draft a Client-Safe Proof Packet outline for the Harbor planning case.

36
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:59,320
State audience, scope, window, inclusions, exclusions, export review, and ledger fields.

37
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:02,780
Redact the course trace in words rather than pasting it.

38
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:15,720
Then make a Foundry Test for the volunteer-coordinator tool: mark each evidence field observed, missing, or unscored; name a payer question, a tiny proposed test, the human gate, and a stop condition.

39
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:18,100
Use a fictional or approved example.

40
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:24,540
Do not use private operational data, contact a person, create a repo, or generate a public claim.

41
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,820
Save revision twelve as a draft.

42
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:18,820
Harbor now has a way to explain its held work and a way to examine a new idea without pretending either is ready to ship.

43
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:21,980
The Operating File keeps the missing evidence visible.

44
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:24,600
That is what makes the next human decision honest.
